in this video we will share some good  news with you we finally have external  primary server that will allow you to  migrate your MySQL server to Google  cloud platform with minimal downtime we  know there are two ways to migrate data  and this talk talks about both but shows  you the new feature the replication from  an external primary into called cycle  the traditional way involves a variable  downtime migration which could take from  minutes to hours or even weeks depending  on the size of your data this approach  usually have the following configuration  first an instance of your database your  primary needs to disconnect from your  application so the data doesn't change  then export this data to a SQL file or  CSV using tools like my C code up or PG  done after that provision a new instance  and import a file export it to this new  server at this point connect to the  application again so the downtime is  over if you can't afford a downtime this  is the simplest way of doing a database  migration if you can't afford that much  downtime there is a different way using  replication on this approach your  application is connecting to an instance  your primary and all the changes are  being set to a new instance of replicas  elsewhere replication will catch up but  you need to stop the application from  continuing writing to the existing  instance once that is completed the  replication is also stopped and the new  instance is promoted to be the new  primary with the promotion process  completed you can now point your  application to read and write to the new  instance watch the session and don't  miss out this feature in action watch as  I migrate the database from a single  instance within a common scenario  running a wordpress application with  apache and mysql to a new scenario where  the database is fully managed by called  sequel leaving the previous instance you  only serve the application  for more interchanges details check out  the full talk and follow the steps also  don't forget to subscribe to our channel  for more great next rewind content  you  [Music]
 

